<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Harry Rawson</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Admiral Rawson</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Harry Rawson was a British admiral who commanded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-expedition-of-1897">Punitive Expedition</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin</a> in 1897. The expedition followed the killing of a British delegation and resulted in the burning of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-city">Benin City</a>, the looting of the palace and the exile of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ovonramwen">Oba Ovonramwen</a>. It ended the independence of the Benin Empire, and the looted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-bronzes">Benin Bronzes</a> were dispersed abroad.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/harry-rawson.jpg" alt="Harry Rawson" width="288" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Freeman Brothers Studio · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Admiral_Sir_Harry_Rawson,_Sydney,_c._1902.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
